\description{
\strong{Play-by-play of one finished B.LEAGUE game, in game order, every feed in one
shape.}

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://b-league.s3.amazonaws.com/web_json/v2_genius_contexts/\{schedule_key\}/\{latest\}.json}
(the v1 feed, or the game page's embed, when v2 does not hold the game).

One row per logged event, oldest first (\code{event_no} ascends; v2 counts in steps of
1000). \code{action}, \code{qualifier2} and \code{qualifier3} are English slugs for the numeric
codes (\code{NA} for a code no sample contains); the team-rebound codes 18 / 19 mean
opposite things on the two feeds and \code{action} follows the \code{feed} column. A v1
substitution is ONE row (\code{action} \code{substitution}, \code{player_id} out, \code{player2_id} in),
a v2 one is two rows (\code{player_out} / \code{player_in}). \code{home_score} / \code{away_score} split
